.hypothesis/
# Scratch directories the run_capture tests write into at run time
# (tests/test_run_capture_action.py, evidence_tmp_dir fixture).
.tdd-evidence/test-runtime/

# Captured pytest output is no longer committed (decided 2026-08-17). A
# saved text file of a failing run is self-reported, so it proves no more
# than one sentence in the commit message, and it costs about 9 KB per
# review finding. Record the red state instead as one line that names the
# test and states how it failed, in the finding's bead comment and in the
# fix commit message. The mutation-gate skill carries the full rule.
#
# The 151 files already tracked stay tracked, because a gitignore entry
# does not affect files git already follows. Several finding beads point
# at them by name, such as "evidence .tdd-evidence/rf23-*".
#
# The pattern covers text files only. A script in this directory can
# still be committed, because a script re-runs and captured output does
# not -- for example rf46-47-mutation-gate.py.
.tdd-evidence/*.txt
